---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Src from '../components/Src.astro';
import Aff from '../components/Aff.astro';
import Unverified from '../components/Unverified.astro';
const S = {
  ttPricing: 'https://www.turbotenant.com/pricing/',
  ttTiming: 'https://support.turbotenant.com/en/articles/4522996-how-long-do-rent-payments-take-to-process',
  ttFaq: 'https://support.turbotenant.com/en/articles/9787222-rent-payments-faqs-for-landlords',
  rrFees: 'https://help.rentredi.com/en/articles/4474091-convenience-fees-for-rent-payments',
  rrFaq: 'https://help.rentredi.com/en/articles/8473991-rentredi-payments-faqs',
  rrPrice: 'https://rentredi.com/pricing/',
  rentec: 'https://www.rentecdirect.com/pricing-transparency',
  rentecPay: 'https://www.rentecdirect.com/details/online-payments',
  rentecKb: 'https://help.rentecdirect.com/article/546-online-payment-processing',
  avail: 'https://www.avail.com/pricing',
};
const updated = '2026-11-21';
const title = 'Rent Collection App Fees Compared: ACH, Card and Payout Times';
const description = 'What TurboTenant, RentRedi, Rentec Direct and Avail charge per online rent payment (bank transfer and card), who pays the fee, and how long it takes the money to reach the landlord. Quoted from each provider\'s pricing and help pages.';
const schema = {"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Article","headline":title,"description":description,"dateModified":updated};
---
<Base title={title} description={description} updated={updated} schema={schema}>
  <h1>{title}</h1>
  <p class="lede">The subscription price is the number on the pricing page. The number that hits every month is the per-payment fee, who it lands on, and how many days the rent sits in transit. Here are those three numbers for four landlord platforms, from their own pricing and help pages as of November 21, 2026.</p>

  <div class="note"><strong>The short version.</strong> Bank transfer (ACH): <strong>TurboTenant</strong> $2 per payment on Free and Essentials, typically waived on Pro <Src href={S.ttTiming} label="TT" />; <strong>RentRedi</strong> $1 <Src href={S.rrFees} label="RR" />; <strong>Rentec Direct</strong> $2 per payment on Starter, one free per property per month on Pro/PM <Src href={S.rentec} label="Rentec" />; <strong>Avail</strong> $2.50 on the free plan, no fee on Unlimited Plus <Src href={S.avail} label="Avail" />. Card fees run 2.95% to 3.5%. Standard ACH payout ranges from about 2 business days (RentRedi, Rentec) to 5–7 (TurboTenant without a paid plan).</div>

  <h2>Side by side</h2>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Platform</th><th>Bank transfer (ACH) fee</th><th>Card fee</th><th>Who pays by default</th><th>Time to landlord's bank</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>TurboTenant</strong></td>
        <td>Free &amp; Essentials: $2 per payment. Pro: "typically waived" <Src href={S.ttTiming} /></td>
        <td>3.49% <Src href={S.ttTiming} /></td>
        <td>ACH fee: landlord on Free/Essentials chooses to cover it (deducted from the deposit) or pass it to the renter <Src href={S.ttTiming} />. Card fee: paid by the tenant and "cannot be waived" <Src href={S.ttFaq} /></td>
        <td>ACH 5–7 business days; 2–4 with Essentials or Pro for eligible payments under $10,000; card 1–3 business days <Src href={S.ttTiming} /></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>RentRedi</strong></td>
        <td>$1.00 per ACH/bank/eCheck payment <Src href={S.rrFees} /></td>
        <td>3.1% + $0.30; debit cards are charged the same as credit <Src href={S.rrFees} /></td>
        <td>Tenant by default. Landlord can cover either fee; it's then deducted from the payment (a $100 ACH payment nets $99) <Src href={S.rrFees} /></td>
        <td>"Typically 2–3 business days to fully process and be deposited"; funds are usually pulled the same day if submitted before 2 PM ET <Src href={S.rrFaq} /></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Rentec Direct</strong></td>
        <td>Starter: $2.00 each incoming payment. Pro &amp; PM: one free incoming ACH per active property per month, extra payments $0.50 each <Src href={S.rentec} /></td>
        <td>Visa/Mastercard/Discover 3.50% on Starter, 2.95% on Pro &amp; PM; AmEx 3.50%; $1.00 minimum <Src href={S.rentec} /></td>
        <td>Rentec's knowledge base says landlords can "customize accepted payment methods and convenience fees" <Src href={S.rentecKb} />. The pricing page lists these as charges for use of the software <Src href={S.rentec} />. Who pays by default: <Unverified /></td>
        <td>ACH "transmitted to your bank account within 2 days"; card payments the next business day; same-day funding available <Src href={S.rentecPay} /></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Avail</strong></td>
        <td>Unlimited (free): tenants pay $2.50 per bank transfer. Unlimited Plus: no fee <Src href={S.avail} /></td>
        <td>3.5% added to tenant payments on either plan <Src href={S.avail} /></td>
        <td>Tenant <Src href={S.avail} /></td>
        <td>Lists "Next-day payment deposits," and "FastPay" on Unlimited Plus <Src href={S.avail} />. Business-day timelines: <Unverified note="not stated on the page we checked" /></td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>

  <h2>Things that change the math</h2>
  <h3>Rentec Direct: two of its pages disagree</h3>
  <p>Rentec's online-payments page says ACH is "free for both parties" <Src href={S.rentecPay} label="Rentec payments page" />, and its knowledge base says tenant ACH payments "do not incur a fee for you or the tenant" <Src href={S.rentecKb} label="Rentec KB" />. Its pricing-transparency page charges $2.00 per incoming payment on the Starter plan and applies a fair-usage rate above one ACH per property per month on Pro and PM <Src href={S.rentec} label="Rentec pricing" />. Read together, "free" seems to describe the Pro and PM allowance, but confirm with Rentec for your plan <Unverified note="our reading" />. Rentec also says you need a business checking account, because "the banks will not transmit rental payments to personal bank accounts" <Src href={S.rentecPay} />.</p>

  <h3>TurboTenant: the fee depends on your plan</h3>
  <p>The renter's ACH fee is $2 unless the landlord is on Pro, where it's typically waived <Src href={S.ttTiming} />. Faster ACH payouts (2–4 business days) need Essentials or Pro and apply only to eligible payments under $10,000 <Src href={S.ttTiming} />. TurboTenant explains that expedited payouts advance the money before the renter's ACH has fully cleared <Src href={S.ttTiming} />. An older TurboTenant FAQ gives card payouts as 2–3 business days rather than 1–3 <Src href={S.ttFaq} label="older FAQ" />; the table uses the October 14, 2026 article.</p>

  <h3>Who absorbs the fee</h3>
  <p>If you cover a per-payment fee, it comes out of the rent. On a $1,500 rent paid by ACH, that's $1 a month on RentRedi or $2 on TurboTenant Free/Essentials (both from the fee pages above). Card fees are percentage-based, so on $1,500 a 3.49% fee is $52.35: that's why most platforms push card fees to the tenant.</p>
  <p>Some states and cities limit fees a landlord can charge tenants. We have not reviewed whether any state restricts passing payment-processing fees to tenants <Unverified note="not yet reviewed" />.</p>

  <h2>Monthly software price</h2>
  <p>For completeness, the subscription each platform publishes: TurboTenant Free $0, Essentials "starting at $12.42/month," Pro "starting at $16.58/month" <Src href={S.ttPricing} />; RentRedi from $12/month on annual billing, $20 on six-month and $29.95 month-to-month <Src href={S.rrPrice} />; Rentec Direct Starter $25/month, Pro and PM a $50 monthly minimum at $2 and $2.50 per unit <Src href={S.rentec} />; Avail Unlimited $0/unit, Unlimited Plus $9/unit per month <Src href={S.avail} />.</p>

